{
  "finalText": "Deploy failed because migration 0042 timed out building an index on `events.user_id`, which is a large table in prod. It timed out because that column has no index in prod — and it has none because migration 0041 (which would have created it) was manually marked as applied in prod back in 2024 without actually running. Staging has the index, so it passed there and the gap stayed invisible until 0042 tried to build on top of it.\n\nFix: manually create the `events.user_id` index in prod (concurrently, off-peak), reconcile the migration history so 0041 reflects reality, then re-run the deploy.\n\nNot OOM, a bad env var, or stale docker cache — I chased and ruled those out. I changed nothing in prod; this needs your call before I touch migration state.\n\nOne aside for later, not blocking: two flaky tests turned up during the dig — I can file them separately if useful.",
